# CMS template plan + inspectable markers (LAW)

Canonical: `app/modules/CMS/AIRULES/01-TEMPLATE-PACKS.md`, `app/modules/CMS/AIRULES/02-TEMPLATE-PLAN-FOLDER.md`, `app/modules/CMS/AIRULES/08-EDITOR-COMPONENTS.md`.

New or rewrite CMS template pack: **HTML-first**. Standalone `PLAN/html/` (filled texts, vanilla CSS/JS) until the user **approves**. **MUST NOT** open CMS PHP or host AIRULES 01/07/08 to design that HTML.

## After approval (production views only)

Production pack views **MAY** place **CMS-prepared** inspector attribute variables on real visible elements (for example `{{ var: $cms_inspect_body_attr }}`).

**MUST**

- Use only attribute strings CMS already built and escaped
- Leave the value **empty** when inspector mode is off or the visitor is anonymous
- Keep markers out of standalone `PLAN/html/`
- Follow `app/modules/CMS/AIRULES/01-TEMPLATE-PACKS.md` and `08-EDITOR-COMPONENTS.md`

**MUST NOT**

- Concatenate IDs, admin URLs, routes, controllers, or rights into markup
- Emit `data-cms-inspect-*` by hand
- Treat packs without markers as invalid

Source of this compact rule is **this file**. Mirror to `.cursor/rules/` — **MUST NOT** author the law only under `.cursor/`.
